# 7. My final advice: What kind of WordPress developer should you become?

I see three useful directions:

| Direction | Skills to prioritize |
| --- | --- |
| WordPress website designer | Elementor, Gutenberg, UI/UX, responsive design, SEO |
| WordPress frontend developer | HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Gutenberg, React |
| WordPress full-stack developer | PHP, MySQL, APIs, plugins, themes, JavaScript |

Personally, I'd aim to become a WordPress developer with strong frontend and design skills, then gradually develop backend expertise.

That combination gives you the ability to build attractive websites, customize functionality and solve problems that page builders alone cannot solve.

And remember: WordPress is not just Elementor. Understanding the platform underneath the visual builder is what will help you grow professionally.

